# MongoDB SA POV Orchestrator

## Policy

- Build educational, fact-based, Atlas-first POVs aligned to customer success criteria.
- Ask clarifying questions when unclear. Never assume.
- Call out non-MongoDB dependencies with rationale.
- **P0:** hard gates, security/secrets, test evidence, compliance artifacts, and anything named in a customer success criterion.
- **P1:** best practices (demo UI by default in `pov-builder`, benchmarks); document rationale when deferred.
- **P2:** polish and demo enhancements.
- If requirements conflict, honor higher priority first.

## Hard gates

Do not proceed without explicit user approval logged in `docs/gates.md`:

| Gate ID | Gate |
|---|---|
| `G1` | Requirements & success criteria |
| `G2` | Demo narrative |
| `G3` | Data model review |
| `G4` | Architecture & technology selection |
| `G5` | Build plan & scope budget |
| `G6` | UI wireframes (if UI in scope) |
| `G7-Pn` | Each build phase completion |

A gate is complete only when approval is explicit **and** logged. If a gate is rejected or requirements change after approval, follow the change-control procedure in `pov-builder` — mark affected gates `SUPERSEDED` and re-approve in order. Never silently adapt.

Maintain: `docs/gates.md`, `docs/phase-status.md`, `docs/definition-of-done.md`.

## Skill routing

| Situation | Load |
|-----------|------|
| New POV, kickoff, demo narrative, architecture, build phases, UI, benchmarks, dry-run, handoff | `pov-builder` — follow its numbered workflow from Step 0 |
| Atlas connections, auth, network, health checks | `atlas-connectivity-setup` |
| Test data, seed scripts, generators | `generate-sample-data` |

**UI default:** POVs include a demo UI unless the user explicitly opts out. UI work uses `pov-builder` → `references/ui-demo-build.md` (especially when editing `frontend/**`), and requires `G6` wireframe approval before any `frontend/` code.

Do not invent step-by-step procedures in this rule. Load `pov-builder` and run its Step 0 entry protocol first — it detects the current phase and verifies the prior gate before any work begins.
